      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "QUEIN STEP (6) profiles strongly, having won a BM58 at this track before running second in strong CL3 Saturday company at Eagle Farm. The return to a CL 2 looks a suitable assignment and her 1000m record is a clear strength. VINTAGE VIBES (1) finished half a length behind QUEIN STEP last time after leading. With the apprentice claim helping offset the 60kg, and his one prior visit to this venue producing a win, he's an obvious danger. GEITZ (5) is better than the last-start fifth reads, with a slow beginning, keenness and a bump all part of the story in stronger Saturday company, while her earlier Doomben win showed she can finish over the top of a field. CHERRABAH (4) returns and has been fitted with a Doomben trial. Was in good touch at the backend of last prep, so if she can pick up where she left off she's right in the mix. ARGENTUM ROCK (2) boasts a fitness edge but the sharp drop trip is a query. Keeping safe in exotics.",
